    "md5": "d912d246e117b61ad049629ce005a51a",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1971,
    "chunk_text": "BE it therefore enacted by the Parliament of the DemocraticSocialist Republic of Sri Lanka as follows:\u2014\n\n1.This Act may be cited as the Daya SaranaDevelopment Foundation (Incorporation) Act,No. of 2013.\n\nIncorporationof DayaSaranaDevelopmentFoundation.\n\n2Daya Sarana Development Foundation (Incorporation)\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n30\n\n3.The general objects for which the Corporation isconstituted are hereby declared to be:\u2014\n\n(a)to promote religious harmony, mutualunderstanding, spiritual development , goodwilland friendship among the youth in the area throughreligious , cultural, educational and economicinteraction;\n\n(b)to protect, support and ensure welfare, interests,safety, integrity and status of people in the area andto safeguard their rights and privileges;\n\n(c)to provide for the physical welfare and personaldevelopment of teenagers through youthdevelopment centers including gumasiums;\n\n(d)to provide additional educational support by givingnecessary training in various fields which willenhance their personal qualification levels in orderto meet the competition and necessary requirementsin finding employment;\n\n(e)to hold and conduct periodical technical trainingcamps for the youth to develop their skills with theultimate aim of projecting them towards findingsuitable employment;\n\n(f)to establish carpentry and masonry and any othersuitable vocational training school in central townsand the like with a view to educate and train youthfor a vocation;\n\n(g)to establish motor mechanism training centers(Garages) in the area in order to train the youth inmotor vehicle repair trade and arrange periodicallectures conducted by professionals in the trade;\n\n(h)to liaise with the Foreign Employemtn Bureau underthe Central Government to facilitate applicationsfrom eligible youth in the area and recommend themfor suitable foreign job opportunities;\n\nGeneralobjects of theCorporation.\n\n3Daya Sarana Development Foundation (Incorporation)\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25"
  },
