    "chunk_text": "(3) The Committee may exercise all the powers of theCorporation to borrow money and to mortgage or charge itsundertaking any property or any part thereof as security forany debt liability or obligation of the Corporation or of anythird party.\n\n(5) The Bank account or Accounts of the Corporationwith any Bank or Banks shall operate and all cheque drawnsigned and endorsed by the President or Vice President orSecretary of the Committee of Management and the Treasurertogether.\n\nIn this preragraph the words \u201cPresident\u201d, \u201cSecretary\u201dand \u201cTreasurer\u201d shall include any acting President,Secretary or Treasurer.\n\n10.(1) The Corporation shall cause proper accounts tobe kept of its income and expenditure, assets and liabilitiesand all other transactions of the Corporation.\n\n(2) The books of Accounts of the Corporation shall bekept at the registered office and open to inspection by everymember of the Corporation.\n\n(3) The Corporation shall have its accounts audited eachaudit year by any qualified public auditor or auditors to benominated at the Annual General Meeting and the auditorsof the corporation shall examine the accounts of thecorporation and furnish a report on the accounts examinedby them and the report shall state :-\n\n(a)whether they have or have not obtained all theinformation and explanations required by them and;\n\nAudit andAccounts.\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n30\n\n9Daya Sarana Development Foundation (Incorporation)\n\n(b)whether accounts of the Corporation are properlydrawn up so as to exhibit a true and fair view of theaffairs of the Corporation;\n\n(c)the accounts will have its legal validity afterauditing and approval of the Committee ofManagement.\n\nIn paragraph the word \u201cQualified Auditor\u201d means\u2014\n\n(a)an individual who being a member of the Instituteof Chartered Accountants Sri Lanka, or of anyother institute established by law, processes acertificate practice as an Accountant issued by suchinstitute; or"
