    "md5": "e0f8d7c93e43c9943e51e28ec95ffa1c",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2015,
    "chunk_text": "(k)to engage in disaste relief and reconstruction;\n\n(l)to establish medical aid and legal aid schemes forthe welfare of people; and\n\n(m)to do all such other thisgs as may be necessary orconducive to the accomplishment of the objects ofthe Corporation.\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n4.(1) The Board of Trustees shall consist of minimumof three and a maximum of seven Trustees, five of whom areappointed in accordance with the rules of the Corporationand others are appointed by the Board of Trustees as andwhen it is deemed necessary,\n\n(2) Mr. Chulapathmendra Dahanayake shall be thelifetime Trustee shall be the Chairman of the Board ofTrustees of the Foundation Trustees for a period of five yearsfrom the date of commencement of this Act.\n\n(3) The other Trustees shall hold office for a period offive years from the date of commencement of this Act.\n\n(4) Any turstee who may be appointed by the Board ofTrustees of the Foundation Trust shall hold office for a periodof five years or less as deermined at the discretion of theBoard of Trustees.\n\n(5) In the event of the death of ChulpathmendraDahanayake the other Trustees shall have the right to elect aperson amongst themselves as Chairman or to appoint a newtrustee in terms of the provision herein contained.\n\n(6) If any Trustees shall retire from office or shall becomeunfit to act or incapable of acting or refuse to act or resign asTrustees or any Trustee shall happen to die, a successorTrustee shall forthwith be appointed by the continuingand / or surviving Trustees provided that any such SuccessorTrustee shall be appointed with the consent of the settlorduring the life.\n\n(7) A Trustee may be removed from office only pursuantto a decision made by a 2/3 majority of the trustees and withthe approval of the settlor.\n\n5.(1) Subject to the provisions of this Act and any otherwritten law the Corporation shall have the power to do allsuch acts and things as are necessary for or conducive orincidental to the carring out of the objects of the FoundationTrust.\n\n30"
