    "chunk_text": "2.Section 28 of the Mines and Minerals Act, No. 33 of1992 (hereinafter referred to as the \u201cprincipal enactment\u201d) ishereby amended by the addition of a new subsectionimmediately after subsection (4) as follows :\u2014\n\n3.Section 33 of the principal enactment is herebyamended in subsection (1) of that section, by the substitutionfor the words \u201cradioactive elements and coral\u201d of the words\u201cradioactive elements, ilmenite, rutile, zircon, garnet,monazite, coral\u201d.\n\n4. Section 64 of the principal enactment is herebyamended as follows :\u2014\n\n(1)in subsection (1) of that section\u2014\n\n(a) in paragraph (m) of that subsection, by thesubstitution for the words \u201cmanner ofcompliance.\u201d of the words \u201cmanner ofcompliance ;\u201d\n\n(b) by the addition at the end of that subsection,of the following paragraphs :\u2014\n\n\u201c(n)specify the minerals required forconstruction purposes ; and\n\nShort title.\n\nAmendmentof section 28of Act, No.33 of 1992.\n\n25\n\nAmendmentof section 33of theprincipalenactment.\n\nAmendmentof section 64of theprincipalenactment.\n\n2Mines and Minerals (Amendment)\n\n5\n\n(o) the capacity, route and methodology oftransport of minerals which require alicence.\u201d.\n\n5.In the event of any inconsistency between the Sinhalaand Tamil texts of this Act, the Sinhala text shall prevail.Sinhala textto prevail inthe event ofanyinconsistency.\n\nMines and Minerals (Amendment)3\n\nAnnual subscription of English Bills and Acts of the Parliament Rs. 885 (Local), Rs. 1,180(Foreign), Payable to the SUPERINTENDENT, GOVERNMENT PUBLICATIONS BUREAU, DEPARTMENT OFGOVERNMENT INFORMATION, NO. 163, KIRULAPONA MAWATHA, POLHENGODA, COLOMBO 05 before 15thDecember each year in respect of the year following."
