    "chunk_text": "PARLIAMENT OF THE DEMOCRATICSOCIALIST REPUBLIC OFSRI LANKA\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\n[Bill No. 232]\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\nPresented by Hon. Prime Minister and Minister of Buddha Sasana andReligious Affairs on March 19, 2013\n\n(Published in the Gazette on February 26, 2013)\n\nOrdered by Parliament to be printed\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\nA\n\nBILL\n\nPRINTED AT THE DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING, SRI LANKA\n\nTO BE PURCHASED AT THE GOVERNMENT PUBLICATIONS BUREAU, COLOMBO 5\n\nPrice : Rs. 3.00Postage : Rs. 5.00\n\n2-2d\n\n2-\n\nDEFENCE SERVICES COMMAND AND STAFFCOLLEGE (AMENDMENT)\n\nto amend the Defence Services Command and Staff College Act, No. 5 of 2008\n\nSTATEMENT OF LEGAL EFFECT\n\nDefence Services Command and Staff College (Amendment) Bill\n\nClause 2 : This clause amends section 7 of the Defence Services Command and StaffCollege Act, No. 5 of 2008 (hereinafter referred to as the \u201cprincipal enactment\u201d) and thelegal effect of the section as amended is to include the Vice-Chancellor of the GeneralSir John Kotelawala Defence University in the Board of Management of the Staff Collegeinstead of the Vice-Chancellor of the University of Kelaniya.\n\nClause 3 : This clause amends section 15 of the principal enactment and the legel effectof the section as amended is consequential to the amendment made by clause 2.\n\n1Defence Services Command andStaff College (Amendment)\n\n2\u2014PL 006981\u2014425 (02/2013)\n\nShort title.\n\nL.D.\u2014O. 17/2012\n\nAN ACT TO AMEND THE DEFENCE SERVICES COMMAND AND STAFFCOLLEGE ACT, NO. 05 OF 2008\n\nBE it enacted by the Parliament of the Democratic SocialistRepublic of Sri Lanka as follows:\u2014\n\n1.This Act may be cited as the DefenceServices Command and Staff College (Amendment) Act,No. of 2013.\n\n2.Section 7 of the Defence Services Command and StaffCollege Act, No. 05 of 2008 (hereinafter referred to as \u201ctheprincipal enactment\u201d) is hereby amended in subsection (1)of that section by the repeal of paragraph (f) of that subsectionand the substitution therefor, of the following paragraph:\u2014"
