    "chunk_text": "BE it therefore enacted by the Parliament of the DemocraticSocialist Republic of Sri Lanka as follows :\u2014\n\n1.This Act may be cited as the Sri BalabhivurdhiWardana Samithiya (Incorporation) Act, No. of 2013.\n\n3.The general objects for which the Corporation isconstituted are hereby declared to be:\u2014\n\n(a)to conduct the annual Poson Maha Peraheraincluding the conduct of the Maha Mahindotsavayato commemorate the memory of Arahath Mahinda,who was instrumental in the setting up of the\n\nPreamble.\n\nIncorporationof the SriBalabhivurdhiWardanaSamithiya.\n\nGeneralobjects of theCorporation.\n\n2Sri Balabhivurdhi Wardana Samithiya(Incorporation)\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n30\n\nBuddha Sasana in Sri Lanka as well as to involve insocial service activities intended for the moral andspiritual development of the youths of the countryin particular and to work towards the upliftmentand all-round development of the hamlet ofWalpola ;\n\n(b)to promote and engage in the implementation ofcommunity welfare, cultural and social developmentprojects in areas within the Walpola village and suchother areas as may be determined by the Samithiya ;\n\n(c)to undertake, the execution of road developmentand housing schemes, the construction andimprovement of hospitals, educational centres,schools, community centres and such other worksand activities as may contribute to the developmentof towns and villages ;\n\n(d)to establish, equip and maintain a pre-school and alibrary ;\n\n(e)to engage in the dissemination of the Dhamma,internationally ;\n\n(f)to preserve and disseminate the BuddhistPhilosophy and the Buddhist way of life ;\n\n(g)to establish friendly relations with other Buddhistorganizations in Sri Lanka and abroad ;\n\n(h)to promote education by establishing andmaintaining pirivenas, schools and othereducational institutions and granting scholarships ;\n\n(i)to provide medical aid, food and housing to thepoor, the destitute and the sick ;\n\n(j)to establish and maintain orphanages and homesfor the aged and to establish social welfare centres ;"
