    "chunk_text": "PARLIAMENT OF THE DEMOCRATICSOCIALIST REPUBLIC OFSRI LANKA\n\nA\n\nBILL\n\nPresented by Hon. Vidura Wickramanayaka, M. P. for Kalutara Districton 08th March, 2012\n\nOrdered by Parliament to be printed\n\nPRINTED AT THE DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING, SRI LANKA\n\nTO BE PURCHASED AT THE GOVERNMENT PUBLICATIONS BUREAU, COLOMBO 5\n\nPrice : Rs. 8.00Postage : Rs. 5.00\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\n[Bill No. 156]\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\n(Published in the Gazette on February 27, 2012)\n\nBULATHSINHALA JANASAKTHI MAHASANGAMAYA(INCORPORATION)\n\nto incorporate the Bulathsinhala Janasakthi Mahasangamaya\n\n2\u2014PL 006628\u2014850 (03/2012)\n\n1Bulathsinhala Janasakthi Mahasangamaya(Incorporation)\n\n2\u2014PL 006595\u2014 75 (02/2012)\n\nPreamble.\n\nShort title.\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\nAN ACT TO INCORPORATE THE COMPUTER SOCIETY OF SRI LANKA\n\nWHEREAS a Society called and known as the \"ComputerSociety of Sri Lanka\" has heretofore been formed in Sri Lankafor the purpose of effectually carrying out its objects andtransacting all matters connected with the said Societyaccording to the rules agreed to by its members:\n\nAND WHEREAS the said Society has hitherto successfullycarried out and transacted the several objects and matters forwhich it was formed and has applied to be incorporated andit will be expedient to grant the said application:\n\nBE it therefore, enacted by the Parliament of the DemocraticSocialist Republic of Sri Lanka as follows :\u2014\n\n1.This Act may be cited as Computer society of SriLanka (Incorporation) Act, No. of 2012.\n\n2.From and after the date of commencement of thisAct, such so many persons as now are members of theComputer Society of Sri Lanka or shall hereafter be admittedas members of the Society hereby constituted, shall be abody corporate with perpectual succession, under the nameand style of the \"Computer Society of Sri Lanka\" ^hereinafterreferred to as the corporation\" and by that name may sue andbe sued, shall have full power and authority to have and usea common seal and to alter the same at its pleasure."
