    "chunk_size_bytes": 1977,
    "chunk_text": "2.From and after the date of commencement of this Act,such and so many persons as now are members of the \u201cRanjithAluvihare Foundation\u201d (hereinafter referred to as the\u201cFoundation\u201d) or shall hereafter be admitted as members ofthe Corporation hereby constituted shall be and become abody corporate (hereinafter referred to as the \u201cCorporation\u201d)with perpetual succession under the name and style of the\u201cRanjith Aluvihare Foundation\u201d and by that name may sueand be sued in all courts, with full power and authority tohave and use a common seal and alter the same at its pleasure.\n\n(a)to promote peace, goodwill, understanding andcooperation among all communities and people ofSri Lanka;\n\nIncorporationof the RanjithAluvihareFoundation.\n\n2Ranjith Aluvihare Foundation(Incorporation)\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n(b)to give assistance, prizes and scholarships to needyschool children to enable them to continue theireducation, encourage them to attend schoolregularly, assist them in their educational,philosophical, religious, cultural and scientificactivities and to establish permanent and mobilelibraries ;\n\n(c)to promote and protect Human rights, Humanvalues, fundamental freedoms, democracy andpluralism in Sri Lanka;\n\n(d)to promote sustainable development in rural andremote areas by utilizing the natural resourcesavailable in those areas;\n\n(e)to promote agricultural, plantation and fisherysectors by introducing latest technologies to obtainmaximum benefits;\n\n(f)to establish information technology centres islandwide for the advancement of scientific studies anddevelopment of the country;\n\n(g)to strengthen Institutes of higher studies, encourageresearches and scholarships for the advancement ofhigher education;\n\n(h)to promote social and cultural activities forenriching the bond between different ethnicitiesand for integrating the Sri Lankan communities;\n\n(i)to empower women, children and the marginalizedgroups such as persons with disabilities, the pooretc.;"
