    "chunk_text": "(g)to promote physical and human resources requiredfor steering the children receiving school educationfor the guidance and additional support of SriLankan academics with the aim of developing theirliteracy and helping them to face publicexaminations;\n\n(h)to assist to develop a good economic condition inthe family by providing the required vocationaltraining, physical and financial resources for youngpeople interested in self employment;\n\n30\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n30\n\n(i)to establish relations with local and foreigninstitutions which have similar aims and objectivesof those of the above Foundation and exchangeresources when necessary and working incollaboration with those institutions;\n\n(j)to print and publish books, journals, hand-outs,newspapers, magazines and distribute the same asper necessities;\n\n(k)to extend full sponsorship and maintainconferences, seminars, workshops and group studyactivities in Sri Lanka and outside for mental,physical, social, moral and intellectualdevelopment activities required for leading a fulllife;\n\n(l)to volunteer promptly to provide whatever servicerequired by patients in hospitals and otherinfirmaries by visiting them and offering themphysical, mental relief;\n\n(m)to intervene immediately for the physical andmental wellbeing of the Sri Lankan people sufferfrom various disasters including natural disastersand make active contribution promptly in whateverrecovery efforts;\n\n(n)to promote individuality by developing attitudesand skills required for stronger, resolute and focusedpublic life by identifying potential powers ofman and paying attention to utilizing suchpotentials for the social and personal advancement;\n\n(o)to organize welfare activities for the betterment offamilies of departed soldiers and make availablethe facilities required for them;\n\n(p)to do all such acts and things as may be necessaryfor the accomplishment of all or any of the objectsof the Corporation.\n\nD. M. Dassanayake Social Services andCharity Foundation (Incorporation)4\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20"
