    "chunk_text": "(3) The allowances and other terms and conditions ofappointment of members of the Advisory Council shall besuch as may be prescribed by the relevant AppropriateAuthority.\n\n17.In this Act, unless the context otherwise requires:\u2014\n\n(a)\u201cAppropriate Authority\u201d means\u2014\n\n(i)in relation to a state school controlled by theGovernment, the \u201cGovernment\u201d; and\n\n(b)\u201cchild\u201d means a child of five years of age on the31st of January of the year of entry;\n\nInterpretation.\n\nRight to Free Education8\n\n(c)\u201cguardian\u201d, in relation to a child, means a personhaving the care and custody of that child andincludes a natural guardian or guardian appointedor declared by a court or a statute;\n\n(d)\u201cMinister\u201d means the Minister in-charge of thesubject of education of the Appropriated Authorityas the case may be;\n\n(e)\u201cprescribed\u201d means prescribed by rules made underthis Act;\n\n(f)\u201cPrescribed Schools\u201d shall mean State schoolscoming under the Government in accordance withitem 3 of List I of the 9th Schedule of theConstitution;\n\n(g)\u201cthe Provincial Executive\u201d means Provincial Boardof Ministers for each Province acting under Article154 (f) of the Constitution or the President or theGovernor or any other person exercising powersunder Article 154 (l) of the Constitution;\n\n(h)\u201cSchedule\u201d means the Schedule annexed to thisAct;\n\n(i)\u201cSchool education\u201d means the education from thegrade one to the grade thirteen subject to any publicexamination.\n\n18.In the event of any inconsistency between theSinhala and Tamil texts of this Act, the Sinhala text shallprevail.\n\nSinhala textto prevail incase ofinconsistency.\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n9Right to Free Education\n\nSCHEDULE\n\n1.The Appropriate Authority recognizes the right of the childto education, and with a view to achieving this right progressivelyand on the basis of equal opportunity, they shall, in particular\u2014\n\n(a)make primary education available free to all;"
