    "chunk_text": "2.From and after the date of commencement of this Act,such and so many persons as now are members of the\u201cSri Lanka Semata Setha Foundation\u201d (hereinafter referredto as the \u201cFoundation\u201d) or shall hereafter be admittedmembers of the Corporation hereby constituted shall be abody corporate, (hereinafter referred to as \u201cthe Corporation\u201d)with perpetual succession under the name and style of \u201cSriLanka Semata Setha Foundation\u201d and by that name may sueand be sued in all courts, with full power and authority tohave and use a common seal and alter the same at its pleasure.\n\n(a)improving the economical standards of the poorfamilies living within Sri Lanka ;\n\nIncorporationof the SriLankaSemata SethaFoundation.\n\n2Sri Lanka Semata Setha Foundation(Incorporation)\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n30\n\n(b)collaborating with the Government activities toimprove and maintain higher standard of educationof these poor families;\n\n(c)supporting the activities to eliminate poverty ofthese families by improving their financialstandards;\n\n(d)supporting the activities of protection of theenvironment in Sri Lanka;\n\n(e)supporting the activities of nutritionalrehabilitation;\n\n(f)joining in collaborative activities with otherorganizations, religious and cultural institutionswhich Foundation the deems necessary to corporatewith ;\n\n(g)assist in the provision of books, instruments,clothing, loans and other financial assistance tochildren in lower income families which needassistance;\n\n(h)to establish a fund and regularize same in order toachieve the above mentioned objectives.; and\n\n(i)to do all other things necessary or expedient for theproper and effective carrying out of the objects ofthe Corporation.\n\n4.Subject to the provisions of this Act, and any otherwritten law, the Corporation shall have the power to \u2014\n\n(a) acquire, hold or take any immovable property forthe corporation or give on lease or hire, mortgage,pledge, sell, exchange or otherwise alienate,encumber or dispose of any immovable property ofthe Corporation;"
